James inquired whether cod is classified as groundfish, to which I confirmed it is, noting that groundfish inhabit the seafloor. He then compared his associations with groundfish, referencing halibut while characterizing cod as more mobile. I elaborated on the differences, explaining that cod are known for their mobility and migratory patterns, swimming in schools and utilizing both horizontal and vertical movements. In contrast, I described halibut as more sedentary, relying on camouflage and remaining close to the seafloor, thereby highlighting the distinction between the two species while confirming both classifications as groundfish.
